{
  "abstract": "An orthonormal terminal frame with k exceptional Schmidt amplitudes has a replacement on 2k coordinates preserving all positive exceptional spectra and all pairs of power-residual exponents simultaneously. With at least k background copies the unnormalized score set stabilizes. For two exceptional amplitudes this gives the attained fixed-state two-step Hardy maximum and an explicit loss below the plastic ceiling for every extra background copy.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Stephanie Alexander"
    }
  ],
